## Combining Variables

You can combine multiple variables in a single command:

```bash
cross-env VAR1=value1 VAR2=value2 VAR3=value3 npm test
```

**Template:**
```bash
cross-env HEADED=true|false CUCUMBER_TAGS="tag_expression" CUCUMBER_WORKERS=number CUCUMBER_PARALLEL=true|false TRACE=all npm test
```

---

## On Windows Command Line (cmd.exe)

If using `cross-env` doesn't work, use Windows-specific syntax:

```cmd
# Set variables first
set HEADED=true
set CUCUMBER_TAGS=@smoke
set CUCUMBER_WORKERS=4

# Then run test
npm test
```

---

## On Windows PowerShell

```powershell
$env:HEADED='true'
$env:CUCUMBER_TAGS='@smoke'
$env:CUCUMBER_WORKERS='4'

npm test
```

